@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+# What is TypeScript?
+
+Same greet function twice. In plain JS, greet(42) explodes at runtime with a TypeError. In TS, the `: string` annotation turns the same bug into a red squiggle before you even save. Superset: all valid JS is valid TS — types are checked, then erased.
